WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:08.559
You guys know that I try my best to stay out
of the day to day political bickering and

00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:13.030
focus more on big ideas and the philosophies
which are behind all the fighting.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:16.419
This doesn't mean I'm completely ignoring
the issue of the moment, be it North Korea,

00:00:16.419 --> 00:00:21.449
the gun debate, or the general state of Trumpism,
but focusing on why people believe what they

00:00:21.449 --> 00:00:26.130
believe is more valuable to me than adding
fuel to the fire of whatever the story of

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.450
the day might be.

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:31.710
Toss in a healthy dose of political gridlock
and we seem to have lots of people who are

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:35.390
yelling but very few people who are doing.

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:39.250
There's one issue happening in American politics
right now which is a great example of the

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:44.050
stagnation we face but that is totally flying
under the radar..

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:50.140
Right now dozens of countries, some of them
key strategic allies, don't have US ambassadors

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:54.870
because the senate has refused voted on their
confirmation.

00:00:54.870 --> 00:01:00.410
Accordingl to the rules right now, the senate
needs 30 hours of debate time to confirm an

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:01.410
ambassadorship.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:06.020
You can imagine with all the nonsensical waste
in DC how impossible it would be to spend

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:11.200
30 hours debating each of the new ambassadorships
when a new administration comes in.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:14.860
We'd be talking about literally thousands
of hours of debate for a branch of government

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:20.810
which can't agree which flavor of yogurt should
be served at the capital hill commissary.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:25.960
Back in 2014, when the Democrats controlled
the Senate, then majority leader Harry Reid

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:31.450
used what is known as "the nuclear option"
to get many Obama appointees through the senate.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:36.061
In effect, Harry Reid changed the rules so
that a simple majority, rather than a 60 vote

00:01:36.061 --> 00:01:41.290
super majority, would be enough to confirm
ambassadors, federal judges and other positions.

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:45.299
Though I was firmly on the Left at the time
and had no issue can I remember with the Obama

00:01:45.299 --> 00:01:49.189
appointees, I was against Reid using such
a drastic tactic.

00:01:49.189 --> 00:01:53.899
To me, if you changed the rules when you're
in power, it's incredibly obvious and probably

00:01:53.899 --> 00:01:58.270
quite deserved when those same rules will
be used against your team when you're not

00:01:58.270 --> 00:01:59.270
in power.

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:04.759
You can righty blame Republicans for not voting
on the Obama appointees in 2014, just as right

00:02:04.759 --> 00:02:10.190
now you can rightly blame democrats for not
voting on Trump appointees in 2018.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:15.220
This is exactly why people rightfully hate
the political machine in Washington.

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:20.320
It either does nothing or it changes the rules
to suit itself while usually leaving the people

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:23.180
its supposed to serve far behind.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:28.389
The Republicans, now led by Majority Leader
Mitch McConnell, could use what is known as

00:02:28.389 --> 00:02:32.880
the Nuclear option right now, just as Reid
and the Democrats did back in 2014.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.980
For whatever reason, McConnell refuses to
do so.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:41.070
Some are saying he has such an old school
affinity for the rules of the Senate, that

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:43.390
he doesn't want to stoop to what Reid did.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:48.500
In a certain way this seems like a principled
position, but at this point in American politics,

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:54.070
I wonder if clinging onto the old ways, while
your your idelogical opponents chisel away

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:59.150
at those very institutions at every opportunity
makes much sense at all.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:04.010
Another wrinkle to this story: is that highest
ranking ambassadorship we have open, Germany,

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:08.180
has been offered to former US spokesman for
the UN, Richard Grennell.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:12.780
Richard is the longest serving UN spokesman
in history, working for four different US

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:13.780
ambassadors.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:16.790
He's also served several other positions in
the government, as well as worked for a few

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:19.140
other high level campaigns.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:23.750
By every measure he is supremely qualified
and I've seen plenty of people on both sides

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:28.910
of the aisle praise him as the type of person
we need more of in politics.

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:32.820
Richard and I have become friends over the
past few years and I can personally tell you

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:36.530
that he's decent guy who truly wants to serve
his country.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:40.490
Oh, and there's one other piece to this: Richard
happens to be gay.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:45.630
You may remember back in 2012 he was briefly
a spokesman for the Romney campaign until

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:51.970
the media decided to attack a openly gay man
for daring to work for the Republican candidate

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:56.620
Mitt Romney thus causing Richard to step down
from the campaign because he didn't want to

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:58.160
be a distraction.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:02.790
Apparently although Romney felt it was just
fine to hire a gay man, and Richard felt it

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:07.530
was totally ok to work for Romney the media
just wouldn't let it be.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:12.680
Gay conservatives like Richard, much like
black conservatives like Larry Elder or women

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:18.120
conservatives like Nikki Haley, challenege
the orthodoxy that the Democrats must own

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:19.660
all of these groups.

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:24.320
I mention Richard's sexuality not because
it is important or even relevant unless you

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:27.290
play the identity politics game as so many
do.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:33.450
In effect, the Democrats are blocking an extremely
qualified, openly gay man from serving his

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:34.450
country.

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:37.040
Aren't the Democrats and Lefties supposed
to be for gays?

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:40.150
Isn't that part of their intersectional word
view?

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:46.220
Immutable characteristics often trump qualifications
if you subscribe to this line of thinking.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:50.520
Shouldn't this also mean supporting gay people
who's political positions you might disagree

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:54.620
with because you believe in their ability
to think for themselves?

00:04:54.620 --> 00:05:00.271
Or perhaps the so-called tolerant side isn't
really pro gay or pro-any minority, they are

00:05:00.271 --> 00:05:04.940
actually on pro those who believe as they
do.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:10.310
Now obviously you know I don't think anyone
should be confirmed because of their sexuality,

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:14.310
nor should their sexuality matter in the least
when it even comes to being nominated in the

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:15.310
first place.

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:19.390
I just think that this particular case is
interesting on so many levels.

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:24.130
We have the gridlock of Washington, with Democrats
refusing to vote on Trump nominees.

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:29.210
We have a majority leader in McConnell that
refuses to use his option to confirm nominees

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:33.300
even though the previous Senate leader Reid
did exactly just that.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:38.520
We have dozens of qualified candidates waiting
to due their civic duty and we have just as

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:43.110
many countries waiting for our ambassadors
to move their and get to work.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:48.260
Caught in all of that mess in a good man,
Richard Grennel, who I happen to know personally,

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:53.490
who doesn't want extra credit for being gay,
but just wants to get to work.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.460
How can you make a difference in all this?

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:59.740
Call your local Senator and ask the assistant
at their office why they aren't voting on

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:00.980
these nominess.

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:06.290
And You can also call Mitch McConnell at his
DC office by calling (202) 224-2541.

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:09.850
Actually, I'm gonna give him a call right
now...

